WEBVTT

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.930
<b>Book 3: Revolution to Change the World</b>

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:22.490
<b>Episode 9: Confidential File 668, Ethereal Love</b>

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.990
I ate a bit of the food.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.080
It's not much, but it's better than nothing.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.950
Tsukishiro was distributing the 
new drug Janome concocted

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.710
to anti-government agitators.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:40.840
Tsuki was killed by a dark shadow.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.090
She was dead by the time I arrived.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.850
I don't know the specifics.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.410
I'm going back to Tokyo now.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.550
We need to track down and deal 
with the drug before it's put to use.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.280
Once you've healed... will you come back?

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.830
I'd like your help.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.630
But I've...

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.000
You won't kill anyone else, 
and we can live together forever.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.710
It's not easy to change...

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.090
But I'd like to make the effort.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:26.740
The score involving the Karasumori 
blood hasn't been settled yet.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.400
I'll be waiting in Tokyo.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.380
That's from when they patched you up.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.470
Who are you?

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.480
It's me, Rinko.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:16.530
Kuzuhara-san pulled out 
all the stops for you.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:20.010
He must really want you alive.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.490
You know Kuzuhara-san?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.990
Yep, on account of me being 
a Nue executioner, too.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.000
You mean I was under 
surveillance the entire time?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.060
You could call it "protection," y'know.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:39.250
You looked like your fangs 
and claws had fallen out.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:43.260
You certainly weren't much of 
a guard when we needed you.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.850
I'm real sorry about what happened to Asahi.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.510
Can't blame you if you hate me...

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.900
Hating you won't turn back the clock.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:59.740
You were watching me under 
Kuzuhara-san's orders?

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.030
You got it.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:05.030
He knew everything all along, then?

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.740
More or less, yeah.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.880
You seem different from before.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.810
You're looking at the real me now.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:20.420
In the village, I had to keep 
a low profile, but now?

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.550
Who's gonna care?

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.920
Don't hold it against me, all right?

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:31.060
It's just what happens when 
I'm forced to stay sober for too long.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.270
By all means, help yourself.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.550
Appreciate it.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.910
So, what'cha wanna do?

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:44.440
If you're headed back 
to Tokyo, I'll tag along.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.700
I've got everything set for the trip.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:04.400
So, we heading back to Tokyo?

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.900
The silent treatment, huh?

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.570
Well, it don't matter where 
you go. I can't lose you.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:18.810
Executioners got a certain scent, see?

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.970
I have nothing left.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.500
No reason to even be alive.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.460
But...

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.710
I don't know.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.380
I don't know what to do.

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:55.550
I know where I should go now.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:05.820
Dunno where you're headed, 
but I know I'm taggin' along.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.230
Let's get a move on!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.950
<b>Temporarily Closed</b>

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:19.040
What the hell else do you 
plan on havin' me do?

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:26.490
That's... No!

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:30.130
Mister, do you know what this means?!

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:36.040
At this point, it should be obvious 
why I brought you here.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:38.390
That stuff costs folks their humanity.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:41.710
There is no such thing.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:44.900
If people cared about their 
humanity in the first place,

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.760
there wouldn't be so much
 misery in the world.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:51.400
That's real rich, comin' from you. 
From a Tokugawa dog.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:55.330
And you're about to throw 
away your humanity

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.040
in order to save your brother's life.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.910
Now do it.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.840
This where you wanted to go?

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.980
No. We're going to be walking another 18 ri.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.660
We come all the way to Tsugaru on a train,

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.940
and you wanna walk until tomorrow morning?

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.440
Where the hell are we headed, anyway?

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.040
My hometown.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:01.820
I have a message from the shogun.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.680
The new drug has been received.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:09.760
Once it has been analyzed and mass-produced, 
you will organize an unstoppable army.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:11.560
This is an urgent matter.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:16.660
You are to deliver the source,
the Karasumori girl, immediately.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.150
That is all.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:20.850
Did the shogun say anything 
about the report I submitted,

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.560
and my recommendations for the drug?

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.960
I wasn't told of anything.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:30.310
Then please tell him that the Karasumori 
girl has too much value as an executor.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:31.960
She can ensure the shogun's safety—

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.460
I'm afraid I can't do that.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:38.140
If you can't, let him know 
I'd like to meet with him.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.730
Humanity has nothing to do with it...

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:48.190
Does it?

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:54.190
I think I've sweated all the
booze out of my system...

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:59.700
You didn't have to accompany me. 
I don't intend on hiding.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.290
Can't do that.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.160
Not like I think you're tryin' to get away, but...

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:13.280
Gotta say, I envy you for having a home,

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.590
even if it's in the middle 
of a buncha mountains.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:21.050
I was being passed around from here 
to there as long as I can remember.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:23.470
Don't even know where I was born.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.090
I was in Mikawa and Owari longer than most,

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:28.440
and I ended up mixing 
the two accents together.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.320
Don't even know what my parents look like.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.980
This is it.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.900
This is the Karasumori village?

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:45.490
Who the heck were these 
Karasumori folks, anyway?

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:51.510
I know they've got something to do 
with the power of the blue blood, but...

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:55.520
From what my mother and father told me,

00:10:55.520 --> 00:11:01.450
the Karasumori clan has been in this 
country for at least 1,600 years.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:05.170
They could sense the presence of Ryumyaku,

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:10.520
picking up and moving along the flow 
of it in order to avoid attention.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.740
Why go to the trouble?

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:14.990
To avoid being pulled into conflicts.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:18.690
The blood of the Karasumori 
clan has the ability

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:21.480
to channel Ryumaku into heightened vitality.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:25.700
Those who became aware of that fact 
tried to turn us into weapons.

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:28.090
There were times in the clan's long history

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:31.740
when we were forced into fighting, as well.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:35.020
But the Karasumori never enjoyed that role.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.210
This a grave?

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:43.220
The villagers are all buried here.

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.720
And my parents...

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:48.570
Do you have anything to eat?

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:50.230
A few rice balls.

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:53.230
The Karasumori sought to avoid conflict,

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.500
and in time, they forgot 
how to fight at all...

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.480
Which is what led to this.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:02.120
I figure some of these folks drank, yeah?

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.240
There were some, yes.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:07.740
Better pour one out for them, then.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:09.240
<b>Blue Pond</b>

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.950
Well, there goes the offering...

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:24.580
It's fine. The Karasumori clan 
always had a kinship with birds.

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:30.900
Can you give me some time by myself?

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:35.550
Got it. I'll be waiting at 
the entrance to the village.

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:42.360
Do you want revenge?

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:44.820
Avenge your clan.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:50.790
As long as even one of our 
clan survives... it won't end.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:53.960
The score involving the Karasumori blood...

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:56.710
...hasn't been settled yet.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:02.460
Nana... When this is all over,

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.220
will you die with me?

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:08.940
That way, we can join my family.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:13.740
With my mother, my father, my brother...

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.310
and where Asahi is.

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:25.780
All done?

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:30.280
There's nowhere I belong. 
But if nothing else...

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:33.100
I can put an end to some unfinished business.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.770
Go ahead and sleep if you want.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:47.450
You haven't slept a wink. 
I'll wake you when we get to Tokyo.

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:50.370
I'm used to not getting much sleep.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.680
Same goes for me.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:56.230
Guess it just comes with the job, huh?

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:01.310
Although I gotta say, I thought living in 
that village would've softened you up.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:05.930
You and Asahi-chan had a real peaceful time.

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:10.950
Came as a real surprise to me.

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:14.000
An executioner living like that...

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.460
Made me think about how
 I'd like to give it a try.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:31.640
Wh-Who are you people?

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.640
No sudden moves, please.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.180
Keep your hands on your knees.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.070
Everyone stay quiet.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:43.980
As long as you follow our 
instructions, you won't be hurt.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:46.220
You, the gentleman in the back of the car.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:52.720
Two cars back, there's an army 
lieutenant-general named Tadaaki Iwasaki.

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:56.670
Let him know that the Deputy Minister of
 Foreign Affairs has been taken hostage,

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:58.110
and bring him here.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:04.270
Everyone else, remain seated. 
If you make a fuss, you will be shot.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.260
Give it a sec.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:12.140
You scum!

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:15.970
Do you think you'll get away with this?!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:20.330
If you value the Deputy Minister's life, 
you'll arrange for our comrade

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.530
to be released from provincial 
prison as soon as possible.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:23.480
What?!

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:26.810
Lt. General Iwasaki, you'll 
disembark at the next station

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:29.820
and deliver our demands 
to the government in Tokyo.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:34.540
If our demands are not met by 
the time we arrive at Tokyo Station,

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:36.730
the Deputy Secretary will be executed.

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:40.260
Where do you terrorist 
filth get the nerve?!

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.340
Draw that sword, and we'll shoot.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:45.710
Iwasaki-kun! Please, stay calm!

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:51.990
You gotta be pretty high up on the ladder 
to even get a ride on this train,

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:54.360
but there are rebels on board?

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:57.970
The English must have paid 
a pretty penny for their fare.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.510
There are few enough that 
I can take them by myself.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.400
Sit your butt down.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:04.980
Aren't you drunk, though?

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.980
Yeah? And?

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:15.280
You there, woman. Don't wander 
around without permission.

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:25.580
How—

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.540
You—

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:37.580
Pretty handy, right?

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:41.980
There are actually forty 
bands of metal inside me.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.830
It's called oronium.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:47.350
And I can make it do whatever I want...

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:51.990
Which makes pretty fast work 
of any guy who gets in my way.

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:58.780
Are you wondering how they got 
forty long strips of metal inside me?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:06.290
They opened me up, keeping me alive, 
and stuffed two strips in per day...

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:09.300
And they kept that up for twenty days.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:12.300
Twenty days of absolute hell!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:19.050
Now, mister, how many do 
you think we can fit in you?

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:34.030
Now, that is good as hell!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.680
Can I hold on to this?

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:41.050
You take it from here.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:43.930
A-Are you from the shogun's personal—

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:46.270
You probably don't wanna 
finish that sentence.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:51.230
Let's say you saved the day, 
okay, Lt. General?

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:57.490
If they're bold enough to pull 
this kinda crap inside a train,

00:17:57.490 --> 00:18:02.520
I don't think shutting down a riot here 
and there is gonna cut it going forward.

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:06.870
Oh, that really hits the spot! 
I oughta drink more Western stuff.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:10.820
That was well done, 
considering you were drunk.

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:14.490
I guess you could say 
I'm a functional drunk?

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:17.660
Or maybe that I do a better job 
when I get a little liquor in me?

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.370
Hey, which is it?

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:23.730
No need for flattery, though.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.710
It probably woulda taken 
you half the time, right?

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.040
Not gonna deny it, eh?

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:34.620
That said, I'm what you 
might call "artificial."

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:37.420
I can wipe the floor with normal folks,

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:40.290
but I can't stack up to 
someone with natural gifts.

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:45.620
Yeah, the execution business 
ain't all fun and games...

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:51.350
But it's not like I know 
any other way to live.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:57.240
<b><i>Morning Dew Used Bookstore</i></b>

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:13.770
<i>You need to clean up properly!</i>

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:19.100
Otherwise customers won't come 
to buy books anymore!

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:34.110
Sorry to bother you, Nana.

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:38.610
I don't plan on opening the store, 
but... if Asahi were here,

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:40.130
she'd want this.

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:53.940
<i>Head back to the bookstore.</i>

00:19:55.400 --> 00:20:00.390
<i>"I hold the world but as the world, Gratiano—</i>

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:04.140
<i>a stage where every man must play a part."</i>

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:08.140
<i>I suppose that was never 
going to be my role...</i>

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:10.560
<i>The Merchant of Venice</i>?<i></i>

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:37.830
You've come.

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:45.470
Here are the details on your next mission.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:48.380
You'll want to give it a look.
